# Files the Shopify CLI must never upload.
#
# Editors write atomically: content goes to `<file>.tmp.<pid>.<hash>` and is then
# renamed over the target. A running `shopify theme dev` watcher can catch that
# temp file mid-write and try to upload it, which Shopify rejects with
# "Must have a .liquid file extension". Harmless, but it looks like a real failure.
*.tmp
*.tmp.*
*.orig
*.rej
*~

# Repo tooling and source data - not theme files
tools/
sample-data/
docs/
.env
